{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791589434,"nonce":"Po1Xsk3OArf/7NJz683A9MdgaU0=","title":"Box shadows with no blur draw wrongly or not at all","message":"ShadowShader, ported from Blinc's sdf_shadow, mishandles outer shadows with zero blur.\n\n**Reproducer**\ntools/snapshot/scenes/ShadowEdges.hx.\n- `box-shadow: 0 0 0 8px green` draws only stray square corners behind the box. The vertex quad grows by blur and offset but not by spread, so the ring falls outside the quad.\n- `box-shadow: 10px 10px 0 blue` draws nothing. The outer branch runs only when blur or spread is non-zero.\n- A spread ring on a square box comes out rounded, because the spread is added to every corner radius. CSS grows a corner by the spread only as far as it is already round: r + s(1 + (r/s - 1)^3) when r \u003c s, so 0 stays 0.\n\n**Fix**\n- Grow the quad by the spread and by one pixel for the antialiased edge.\n- Draw outer shadows whatever the blur and spread are.\n- Antialias hard edges over a pixel, inset ones too, instead of stepping at the edge.\n- Use CSS's spread radius.\n\n**Elsewhere**\nblinc_ts's TypeGPU shadow shader is a port of the same code and has the same defects; it was found there first. Blinc's own sdf_shadow.wgsl likely has them too.","files":null}]}